        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "b08d9e4c-8197-5441-82e6-e37a4545f255",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Pocahontas, The Game Plan, America's Heart and Soul, The Little Mermaid, Aladdin, Dinosaur, Home on the Range, The Prince and the Pauper\n- People: H. Lee Peterson, Andy Fickman, Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price, Audrey Wells, Dwayne \"The Rock\" Johnson\n- Companies: Walt Disney Feature Animation, Walt Disney Pictures, Blacklight Films\n- Topics: film credits, film production, film editing\n\nFacts:\n- Pocahontas is a 1995 American animated musical romantic-comedy-drama film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was an assistant editor for The Little Mermaid.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Aladdin.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Pocahontas.\n- America's Heart and Soul is a 2004 film produced by Blacklight Films and released by Walt Disney Pictures.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Dinosaur.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for Home on the Range.\n- The Game Plan is a 2007 American family comedy film directed by Andy Fickman, written by Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price, and Audrey Wells, and starring Dwayne \"The Rock\" Johnson.\n- The Game Plan was the last film in which Dwayne \"The Rock\" Johnson used the ring name \"The Rock\" in billing.\n- H. Lee Peterson was the lead film editor for the short film The Prince and the Pauper, which starred Mickey Mouse.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "80eae63a-5876-52fd-879d-ae57f5864c94",
        "text": "Page: Pocahontas (1995 film). Sentence: Pocahontas is a 1995 American animated musical romantic-comedy-drama film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation for Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: The Game Plan (film). Sentence: The Game Plan is a 2007 American family comedy film directed by Andy Fickman and written by Nichole Millard, Kathryn Price and Audrey Wells and starring Dwayne \"The Rock\" Johnson (marking the last film in which Johnson uses his ring name \"The Rock\" in billing).\nPage: H. Lee Peterson. Sentence: His credits for Walt Disney Pictures include being an assistant editor for \"The Little Mermaid\", and the lead film editor for \"Aladdin\", \"Pocahontas\", \"Dinosaur\", \"Home on the Range\" and the short film \"The Prince and the Pauper; starring Mickey Mouse\".\nPage: America's Heart and Soul. Sentence: America's Heart and Soul is a 2004 film produced by Blacklight Films and released by Walt Disney Pictures.",
